# arvo-strategy. Backlog

## Tracked bridge expansions

Const-trait substrate bridges deferred from round 202605021800 (Round 1)
to later rounds within PR #42:

- ConstFrom\<T\> / ConstTryFrom\<T, E\> substrate bridge. Replaces
  non-const stdlib From::from / TryFrom::try_from for in-substrate
  const-context conversion. Lands in Round 4 (#314). Surfaces from
  Expert B Finding 8.
- ConstDeref / ConstAsRef\<T\> substrate bridge, placed in
  arvo-transparent. Replaces non-const stdlib Deref::deref /
  AsRef::as_ref for transparent-newtype const-projection. Lands in
  Round 4 (#314). Surfaces from Expert B Findings 6, 24.
- ConstTry / ConstControlFlow\<R, O\>. Replaces non-const stdlib
  Try / FromResidual for ? on Bool in const context. Lands in
  Round 5 (#315). Surfaces from Expert B Finding 21.
- ConstHash / ConstHasher (in arvo-hash). Replaces non-const stdlib
  Hash::hash for compile-time content addressing. Lands in
  Round 5 (#315). Surfaces from Expert B Finding 40.

Each bridge follows the same pattern as ConstEq / ConstDefault
shipped in Round 1: a substrate-owned const trait alongside the
stdlib trait (which stays for boundary coverage). Consumer code
imports the substrate bridge to compose const-callable substrate
operations.

